![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Declaring `overlayEntry` as `late final` and initializing it inside the `Overlay` constructor can lead to a confusing `LateInitializationError` in `addTearDown` if an exception is thrown during the test setup (before `overlayEntry` is assigned). 

To make the test more robust and avoid `late` variables, we can define and initialize `overlayEntry` first, register it in `addTearDown`, and then pass it to the `Overlay` widget.

```dart
      const overlayChildKey = ValueKey<String>('overlay child');
      double dimension = 100;
      final OverlayEntry overlayEntry = OverlayEntry(
        canSizeOverlay: true,
        builder: (BuildContext context) {
          return SizedBox.square(
            dimension: dimension,
            child: Center(
              child: OverlayPortal(
                controller: controller,
                overlayChildBuilder: (BuildContext context) =>
                    const SizedBox(key: overlayChildKey),
                child: const SizedBox.square(dimension: 40),
              ),
            ),
          );
        },
      );
      addTearDown(
        () => overlayEntry
          ..remove()
          ..dispose(),
      );
      final Widget overlay = Overlay(
        alwaysSizeToContent: bounded,
        initialEntries: <OverlayEntry>[
          overlayEntry,
        ],
      );
```

