![critical](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/critical.svg)

Using `VoidCallback` (which is `void (*)(void)`) for `destruction_callback` is a critical issue. Since the callback is invoked with `user_data` (a `void*` argument) in `EmbedderExternalTextureSourceVulkan::~EmbedderExternalTextureSourceVulkan()`, and is assigned to `SkImages::TextureReleaseProc` (which is `void (*)(void*)`), this signature mismatch is undefined behavior. On platforms with Control Flow Integrity (CFI) enabled, calling a function pointer with a mismatched signature will cause an immediate crash.

We should define the callback signature to accept `void*` directly.

```c
  /// Callback invoked (on an engine managed thread) that asks the embedder to
  /// collect the texture.
  void (*destruction_callback)(void* user_data);
```

