![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

When `freeze` is `true`, the texture should not resolve a new frame from the embedder. Currently, if `last_image_` is `nullptr`, `ResolveTexture` is called regardless of the `freeze` parameter. We should check `!freeze` before resolving the texture, consistent with the OpenGL and Metal external texture implementations.

```suggestion
  if (last_image_ == nullptr && !freeze) {
    last_image_ =
        ResolveTexture(Id(), context.gr_context, context.aiks_context,
                       SkISize::Make(bounds.GetWidth(), bounds.GetHeight()));
  }
```

![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

`CreateCommandBuffer()` can return `nullptr` if the context is in a bad state or being disposed. We should check if `buffer` is null before dereferencing it to cast to `CommandBufferVK`.

```suggestion
    auto buffer = impeller_context.CreateCommandBuffer();
    if (!buffer) {
      return nullptr;
    }
    impeller::CommandBufferVK& buffer_vk =
        impeller::CommandBufferVK::Cast(*buffer);
```

